          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here is a practical upgrade plan. Since we are in Plan mode, I’m not changing files yet; this is the roadmap we can implement once you switch to the Code agent.\n\n## Goal\nTurn the current working prototype into a production-capable platform with:\n- Real, unique worker IDs\n- Real phone OTP verification\n- A real AI chatbot\n- All 22 scheduled Indian languages\n- Better UI/icons/animations\n- Strong offline support\n\n## 1. Real Worker IDs\n**Current issue:** the demo account uses a fixed `SS-10428`, which feels fake.\n\n**Plan:**\n- Generate IDs with a secure format such as `SS-2026-AB12CD` using `crypto.randomBytes`, with a database uniqueness check.\n- Store each ID in a `workers`/`users` registry with status: `active`, `suspended`, `revoked`.\n- Make the QR code contain a signed verification token, not just the WID, so IDs cannot be forged or guessed.\n- Add admin actions: issue, reissue, revoke, and audit log.\n- Keep one clearly labeled demo account only for testing, or remove it entirely in production.\n\n**New backend pieces:**\n- `src/services/id-service.js`\n- `src/routes/identity.js` enhancements\n- Migration from JSON files to SQLite/PostgreSQL\n\n## 2. Real Phone Verification\n**Current state:** OTP is generated locally and shown on screen.\n\n**Plan:**\n- Add an SMS provider abstraction:\n  - MSG91 / Twilio / Fast2SMS\n  - Environment-based provider selection\n  - Dev fallback only when no provider is configured\n- Store only hashed OTPs with expiry, attempts, IP, and device metadata.\n- Add rate limits: resend cooldown, max attempts, daily send cap.\n- Verify ownership before linking phone to account.\n- Allow login by verified phone plus password or OTP-only login.\n- Add audit logs for send/verify/fail events.\n\n**Security additions:**\n- CAPTCHA or device fingerprint for repeated sends\n- Brute-force lockout\n- HTTPS-only cookies in production\n\n## 3. AI Chatbot\n**Current state:** deterministic rule-based assistant.\n\n**Plan:**\n- Keep the rule-based engine as the offline fallback.\n- Add an optional LLM provider layer:\n  - OpenAI / Gemini / Anthropic / self-hosted model\n  - Environment keys only; no key required for fallback mode\n- Add retrieval over your own content:\n  - safety guidance\n  - schemes\n  - camps\n  - emergency steps\n- Store conversation history per user with privacy controls.\n- Add safety guardrails:\n  - no medical diagnosis\n  - emergency escalation\n  - harmful-content filtering\n- Support streaming responses for better UX.\n\n**Offline behavior:**\n- Cache recent answers\n- Fall back to local rules\n- Queue unanswered questions for later sync if needed\n\n## 4. All 22 Scheduled Indian Languages\nThe 22 languages are: Assamese, Bengali, Bodo, Dogri, Gujarati, Hindi, Kannada, Kashmiri, Konkani, Maithili, Malayalam, Manipuri, Marathi, Nepali, Odia, Punjabi, Sanskrit, Santali, Sindhi, Tamil, Telugu, Urdu.\n\n**Plan:**\n- Build a real i18n system with locale files for all 22 languages.\n- Add language selector in onboarding and profile.\n- Store user language preference.\n- Translate:\n  - UI labels\n  - scheme summaries\n  - safety lessons\n  - AI system prompts\n  - voice input/output language codes\n- Handle RTL for Urdu where needed.\n- Use LLM or translation API for content localization, then human review for critical safety text.\n- Add fallback chain: selected language → Hindi → English.\n\n**Voice support:**\n- Web Speech API language codes where available\n- Text fallback for unsupported browsers/devices\n\n## 5. Better UI, Icons, and Animations\n**Current issue:** emoji/Unicode-like icons and basic transitions.\n\n**Plan:**\n- Replace symbols with a self-hosted SVG icon set, such as Lucide or Phosphor.\n- Create a design token system:\n  - colors\n  - spacing\n  - typography\n  - motion\n- Add purposeful animations:\n  - page transitions\n  - card entrance\n  - loading skeletons\n  - success states\n  - SOS urgency animation\n- Respect `prefers-reduced-