ent/src/lib/firebase-phone.ts`.\n- Move the fetch wrapper (auth header, offline cache, queue-on-failure) into `client/src/lib/api.ts`.\n- Add Vitest unit tests for `offline.ts` and `api.ts` (reusing the patterns from `tests/api.test.js`).\n- **Checkpoint:** data layer usable from a React component; vanilla app still runs in parallel.\n\n## Phase 3 — Service worker strategy\n- Move `public/sw.js` → `client/public/sw.js` and add the `self.__WB_MANIFEST` placeholder so `vite-plugin-pwa` (`injectManifest` strategy) can inject the precache list at build time.\n- Keep all custom runtime logic (background sync, IDB flush, cache fallback) untouched.\n- Register the SW in `main.tsx` with `navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')`.\n- Verify offline mode works on the built app: cached dashboard loads, POSTs queue, background sync fires on reconnect.\n- **Checkpoint:** PWA behavior identical to today, but built by Vite.\n\n## Phase 4 — Incremental page migration\nRecommended order (simplest → most complex), one page per PR/commit:\n\n1. **Offline & Sync** (`/offline`) — simplest: reads the queue from IDB, shows pending actions, manual sync button. Proves routing + IndexedDB integration end-to-end.\n2. **Privacy** (`/privacy`) — toggles persisted via `/user/privacy`; simple form.\n3. **Help & FAQ** (`/help`) — mostly static content.\n4. **Auth** (`/auth`, `/signup`, `/otp`) — login/signup/verify flows; needed before the rest.\n5. **Home** (`/home`) — hero, quick tiles, recent collections, progress.\n6. **Recycling centres** (`/recyclers`) — map panel, centre cards, geolocation.\n7. **AI Saathi** (`/ai`) — chat, voice, suggestion chips.\n8. **Safety / Scanner / Checklist / Training / Guide / Incident / SOS**.\n9. **Work pages** (collections, history, progress).\n10. **Identity** (digital ID, verify, profile, phone verification).\n11. **Opportunities** (benefits, health camps, community).\n12. **Admin** (MCD centre).\n\nEach page migration includes: porting its render/mount logic to a React component, replacing `SS.go()` with React Router `navigate()`, replacing `SS.api()` with the new `api.ts`, and adding a smoke test.\n\n## Phase 5 — Decommission vanilla\n- Once all routes are migrated and verified, delete `public/app.js`, `public/js/`, `public/styles.css` (keep `icon.svg`, `manifest.webmanifest`).\n- Remove the old hash-router; React Router owns navigation.\n- Update `vercel.json` to drop the now-unused static fallback (SPA fallback already in place).\n- Run the full test suite + a manual offline/PWA audit.\n\n---\n\n## Folder-structure rationale\n- `client/` is isolated so the Node backend (`src/`, `api/`, `tests/`) stays untouched and Vercel can build/deploy both halves independently.\n- `client/src/lib/db/offline.ts` keeps the IndexedDB schema and logic byte-for-byte equivalent (same store names, key paths, and queue item shape), so cached data from the old app remains readable during the transition.\n- `client/src/components/ui/` holds shadcn components; feature components live in `client/src/components/` and pages in `client/src/routes/`.\n\n## Recommended first page to migrate\n**`/offline` (Offline & Sync)** — it's the smallest page, it directly exercises the IndexedDB data layer we're preserving, and it lets us validate routing + the new `api.ts` + the service worker in one shot before touching anything user-facing.\n\n## Risks & mitigations\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| Offline behavior lost mid-migration | Keep `public/sw.js` running until Phase 5; new app and old app share the same SW registration path. |\n| Data loss during IDB module move | Keep store names/key paths identical; add a hydration test that reads old-format data. |\n| Vercel build config | Validate Phase 1 scaffold on a preview deploy before migrating any page. |\n| i18n regressions | Port dictionaries verbatim first; translate component strings only after. |\n| Heavy features (DnD, charts) | Add them only after the core pages are migrated (post-Phase 4